WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.434
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-winning

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.334
writer, actor, and comedian.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:06.868
New episodes of
"The Sarah Silverman Podcast"

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:08.100
are released on Thursdays.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.701
She also stars in the new show,
"Santa Inc.,"

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.934
which premieres
on HBO Max December 2nd.

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:14.968
Please become back to the show,
our very good friend,

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:16.133
Sarah Silverman, everybody.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:18.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:25.567
♪♪

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:28.901
[ Cheering intensifies ]

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:31.467
-Welcome back to the show,
Sarah.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.701
-Well, thank you.
-We've seen each other a lot

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:35.067
virtually,
but we were saying backstage,

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:36.334
it's nice to see each other
in person.

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:38.868
-I know. It's weird.
It felt like I had seen you.

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:40.033
-But yet, we hadn't.
-Yeah.

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:41.267
-But you have
some very big news.

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:44.133
You moved into a house.
-Big news, everybody!

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.567
I bought a house!
-That's right.

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:47.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:49.834
I've never --
I grew up in New Hampshire.

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:50.968
I lived in a house.
-Yeah.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.367
-But I have never lived
in a house

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:55.200
since leaving New Hampshire.
And I never thought I would.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.601
I thought I was an apartment
person, but I'm a house person.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:59.300
-Yeah.
And it's a big --

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.968
I mean, the biggest step,
I would imagine,

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:03.567
is the amount of things
that go wrong, right?

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:05.267
-Well, I've always --
when I come home,

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:10.200
even in my apartment, I --
I always go, "Hello? Hello?"

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:14.167
'Cause I get scared,
and I look under the bed,

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:16.334
and I look in the closet,
"Hello? Hello?!"

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:17.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.868
I don't even just
want to sound like a man,

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:22.100
I want to sound like --
like I'm a deranged person.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.601
[ Laughter ]
"Hello?!"

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:25.167
I don't know what I think
is gonna happen.

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:27.667
Like, they're gonna be like,
"This guy's crazy.

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:28.901
Let's get out of here."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:30.934
I don't know.
But it makes me feel better.

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:32.567
-So you have more hellos to say,
I would guess,

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:33.634
in a bigger house.
-"Hello?! Hello?!"

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.100
More around, yeah.
"Hello? Hello?!"

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:38.133
-Still no answers.
You've never gotten

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:39.601
a response to the hellos.
-Oh, my God.

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:42.334
That would be so scary.
-Someone's like, "Hello."

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:43.434
Like, some --
But especially this --

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:45.634
-"Aah!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:47.634
If they said it like they've
just been waiting for someone,

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.334
say it like, "Hi!"
-Yeah.

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:51.934
"Hi!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.400
Oh, my God.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.968
Is it -- Is it like the kind of
thing where you've got to, like,

00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:58.434
mow lawns and stuff?

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:00.701
-I mean, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:02.567
A little bit.
-Congratulations on that.

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:05.667
-I don't know why that reminds
me of -- this is what

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.968
the old Chappelle joke
about when he first, like,

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:11.334
went out to -- he went --

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:13.234
when he first went
to Los Angeles years ago --

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:14.834
I've known him
since he was 17 --

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:18.801
and he went -- he went to L.A.,
and he'd heard all this, like,

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.801
rap music about South Central
and everything,

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:21.968
and then he got there

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:23.467
and people were mowing lawns,
you know?

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:25.434
He was like,
"People have lawns."

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:27.701
Anyway, that's not
what I'm here to talk about.

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:29.000
-Do you --
-Yeah, I --

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.467
-Is it a busy area,
or is it like -- is it like a --

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:33.968
-No. It's --
It's out in the middle of --

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:37.100
It's, like, in a canyon with --
I mean, I can still, like,

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.734
order Carl's Jr.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:42.100
Carl Jr.'s,
as it should be called.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.367
[ Laughter ]
But then there's like --

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:45.734
-Wait. You believe it
should be Carl Jr.'s?

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:48.400
-Shouldn't it be Carl Jr.'s?
-All right.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:52.167
No, I see your point.
'Cause, otherwise, it's like,

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:53.968
"Who's this Jr.
that belongs to Carl?"

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:55.133
Is that what you're saying?
-Yeah. It's like,

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:58.934
"What's that surgeon general --
No --

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:01.033
-Oh, yeah.
Surgeons general.

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:02.234
-Yeah, it's like that.
-Yeah.

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:05.067
-What, is the surgeons general,
this Carl's Jr.?

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:06.534
Come on.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.033
Anyway...

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:09.300
[ Laughter ]
I'm gonna die on that hill.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.868
-This is what you're here
to talk about.

00:03:10.868 --> 00:03:12.434
-That's what I'm here
to talk about.

00:03:12.434 --> 00:03:14.767
-You got sidetracked
on the Dave Chappelle

00:03:14.767 --> 00:03:17.033
lawn story, but now --
now we're into the meat of it.

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:18.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:21.667
-But -- it is like
I could order in, but also,

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:25.534
it is, like, nature and --
I mean, it's --

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:28.200
there's a skunk
that always comes by,

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.434
and we call him,
Trip Skunkerton.

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:33.267
-Trip --
-'Cause he's the third.

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:34.701
[ Laughter ]
Anyway...

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:38.934
And there's, like,
coyotes and mountain lions.

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:41.834
Oh, and I was reading --
do you know how you get a bear?

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:44.534
Like, if you encounter a bear --
This is good to know.

00:03:44.534 --> 00:03:46.701
-Yeah.
-All right, you're supposed

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:49.033
to make yourself
as big as possible.

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:51.701
-Uh-huh.
-And then you make a loud noise

00:03:51.701 --> 00:03:53.834
while you --
while you walk back.

00:03:53.834 --> 00:03:55.467
You know, back up from it.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:58.634
-So you go --
[ Roars ]

00:03:58.634 --> 00:03:59.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:03.534
Like that.
-I feel like --

00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:05.100
I don't know.
I feel like a bear

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.267
came up with that.

00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:08.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:11.667
Right?

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:12.968
-Oh, my God.

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:15.734
Bears are just trying
to make us look like ass [bleep]

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:17.767
[ Laughter ]
You're so smart.

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:19.734
-Then they just go back
to the cave, and they're like,

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:22.400
"It happened again."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.634
"That lady."
"Which lady?

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:24.901
The one who says 'hello'
when she comes home?"

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:27.367
"Yeah."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.234
She made herself real big,
slowly walked back,

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:32.968
tripped over this skunk.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:35.000
You -- We've talked about
your dog before.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.767
Dog's name is --
-Mary.

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:39.334
You know what?
My dog's name is Mary.

00:04:39.334 --> 00:04:41.901
And -- I -- We were just talking
in the dressing room, like --

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:45.033
Everyone has --
Like, the guy who did my makeup,

00:04:45.033 --> 00:04:47.901
Quinn, his dog is Carol.
-Yeah.

00:04:47.901 --> 00:04:49.801
-You know, like, everyone
has people's names now.

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:52.334
So now I just feel like --
when I meet people

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:54.734
at the dog park, and it's like,
"This is Carol."

00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:57.000
"This is Mary," I feel like
going, like, "I'm Puddles."

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:03.067
"This is my boyfriend, Shadow."
You know, like, whatever.

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:04.834
Anyway...
-Can I say something about Mary?

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:06.767
-Yes.
-Beautiful teeth.

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:11.267
Just -- like, you don't often
see dogs with teeth this pretty.

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:13.133
-Okay.
Is this a big reveal?

00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:14.734
Well, she got
eight teeth removed.

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:18.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:20.968
She had a big underbite.
She got eight teeth removed.

00:05:20.968 --> 00:05:22.601
-I like that you said,
"Is this a big reveal?"

00:05:22.601 --> 00:05:24.801
You sent these pictures.
I don't --

00:05:24.801 --> 00:05:26.667
-I know, but I --
there are some pictures

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:28.167
where she has teeth.
-She looks -- She actually does.

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:30.300
Her teeth look good there, yeah.
-You can see her teeth there.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.701
-Yeah.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:05:31.701 --> 00:05:33.167
-Yeah. She's like --

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:35.234
I don't even know
what kind of animal she is.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.334
-Yeah.
-She's definitely not

00:05:37.334 --> 00:05:39.167
a guard dog, obviously.
-Right.

00:05:39.167 --> 00:05:42.801
-But I still feel like,
if murderers come in,

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:45.067
she will immediately
go on her back and be like,

00:05:45.067 --> 00:05:46.400
"Rub my belly."
-Yeah.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.267
-But I still feel like
that will do something.

00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:51.200
Like, I can just picture
murderers going like,

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.467
"Aww.
What are we doing?"

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:56.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.133 --> 00:05:57.734
But, you know,
when you don't have kids --

00:05:57.734 --> 00:05:59.634
Like, you have kids,
but when you don't have kids,

00:05:59.634 --> 00:06:02.467
your dog is your child,
you know?

00:06:02.467 --> 00:06:06.634
It's your baby that you -- but
that you want to die before you.

00:06:06.634 --> 00:06:08.200
That's the only caveat.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:11.000
-Yeah. Oh, that's
a massive difference, yeah.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.934
-It's a bit of a difference,
yeah.

00:06:12.934 --> 00:06:15.567
-But I -- I follow the logic,
of course, yeah.

00:06:15.567 --> 00:06:17.968
No one ever loves a dog enough
that they're like,

00:06:17.968 --> 00:06:20.133
"I hope I go first."
-You never want --

00:06:20.133 --> 00:06:22.801
Yeah, I mean,
it's still the natural order.

00:06:22.801 --> 00:06:24.467
-Yeah.
All right.

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:26.100
Well, I hope Mary's
not watching.

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.400
[ Laughter ]
-She's not.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.167
-It would be very jarring.
-She hates your show.

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:31.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.367
I disagree. I mean...
-We'll be --

00:06:33.367 --> 00:06:35.234
-She's a big Trump-head.

00:06:35.234 --> 00:06:37.968
-We'll be right back with more
from Sarah Silverman.

